"public","site_admin":false},"body":"That makes sense to me, as long as we add a comment to explain why it's done. I don't see why we'd ever want particles to collide with editor-only layers.","created_at":"2025-01-25T22:43:16Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T22:43:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101947#discussion_r1929621190","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101947","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1929621190"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101947#discussion_r1929621190"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101947"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1929621190/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":3992,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1929577966,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1932971500","pull_request_review_id":2579590282,"id":1932971500,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5zNs3s","diff_hunk":"@@ -3988,6 +3988,11 @@ void RendererSceneCull::render_particle_colliders() {\n \t\t\t\tif (!instance || !((1 << instance->base_type) & (RS::INSTANCE_GEOMETRY_MASK & (~(1 << RS::INSTANCE_PARTICLES))))) { //all but particles to avoid self collision\n \t\t\t\t\tcontinue;\n \t\t\t\t}\n+\n+\t\t\t\tif (!(instance->layer_mask & RSG::particles_storage->particles_collision_get_cull_mask(hfpc->base) & ((1 << 20) - 1))) { //forces editor/gizmo layers to be ignored","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp","commit_id":"b162c59097e7771e8d8d62df9b705b13ef770901","original_commit_id":"8115065c1be65f953b5ec01ac7df2ecc4c7aa200","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"We shouldn't have editor hacks inside the Rendering Server. \r\n\r\nInstead what we should do is set the change the cull mask from the editor if that is possible. Maybe in the gizmo code for ParticleCollisions.\r\n\r\nBasically the problem comes from the fact that, for some reason, particle collisions default to enabling all 32 bits for the cull mask\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a013481b0911e59cc3f3dea7ebb732450c3e1460/scene/3d/gpu_particles_collision_3d.h#L40\r\n\r\nWhile everything else only uses the first 20 bits. \r\n\r\nYour code here masks out those 20 bits making them not usable. Which unfortunately, technically breaks compatibility. The original logic for `cull_mask` can be found in the docs for [Camera3D](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_camera3d.html#class-camera3d-property-cull-mask):\r\n\r\n> Note: Since the [cull_mask](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_camera3d.html#class-camera3d-property-cull-mask) allows for 32 layers to be stored in total, there are an additional 12 layers that are only used internally by the engine and aren't exposed in the editor. Setting [cull_mask](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_camera3d.html#class-camera3d-property-cull-mask) using a script allows you to toggle those reserved layers, which can be useful for editor plugins.\r\n\r\nSo basically the logic is, only expose 20 by default. If users want to use more than 20 they can, but they do so at their own risk. Accordingly, we should respect those extra 12 bits. \r\n\r\nFor ParticleCollisions, the situation is much worse because we expose all 32 bits by default. \r\n\r\n_Edit: To be clear, if we can't reliably alter the cull mask only in the editor from the editor code, then I think the best option might be to go back to changing the default :( I would really like to avoid that, but after doing some more investigation it might be inevitable_","created_at":"2025-01-28T22:53:53Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T22:58:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101947#discussion_r1932971500","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101947","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1932971500"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101947#discussion_r1932971500"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101947"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1932971500/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":3992,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938323489","pull_request_review_id":2574185779,"id":1938323489,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ziHgh","diff_hunk":"@@ -2893,6 +2893,13 @@\n \t\t\t\tSets the signed distance field [param texture] for the 3D GPU particles collision specified by the [param particles_collision] RID. Equivalent to [member GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.texture] or [member GPUParticlesAttractorVectorField3D.texture] depending on the [param particles_collision] type.\n \t\t\t</description>\n \t\t</method>\n+\t\t<method name=\"particles_collision_set_height_field_mask\">\n+\t\t\t<return type=\"void\" />\n+\t\t\t<param index=\"0\" name=\"particles_collision\" type=\"RID\" />\n+\t\t\t<param index=\"1\" name=\"mask\" type=\"int\" />\n+\t\t\t<description>","path":"doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml","commit_id":"b162c59097e7771e8d8d62df9b705b13ef770901","original_commit_id":"e3508c4d800c16daa1f8242f0c4469aa06b79e72","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Needs a description","created_at":"2025-02-01T18:35:44Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T18:36:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101947#discussion_r1938323489","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101947","_links":{"self":{